WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.889
Congratulations, you just beat Resident Evil
7.

00:00:03.889 --> 00:00:08.630
The credits are rolling and other then trying
the game in VR after seeing a video about

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:11.920
it on the internet, you’ve experienced all
there is to the game.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:12.920
Right?

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:13.920
Wrong!

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:17.600
Because you just unlocked madhouse difficulty
and it's much more than just a difficulty

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:18.600
bump.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:22.689
It changes the game and plays with your expectations
in some pretty cool ways.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:27.779
I can’t resist a promise like that so let’s
find out how different Madhouse really is.

00:00:27.779 --> 00:00:31.720
By the way I am going to talk openly about
the first section of the game up until you

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:36.110
leave the main house so if you don't want
to hear any spoilers or you want to experience

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:40.391
madhouse blind, pause this video, subscribe
so you don’t forget, play the game, and

00:00:40.391 --> 00:00:41.399
then come back and watch.

00:00:41.399 --> 00:00:54.559
Let’s do this.

00:00:54.559 --> 00:00:59.250
The first and most important difference you’ll
notice is when you get to your first save.

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:03.129
Saves in madhouse are limited just like in
the original Resident Evil, except instead

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:06.250
of finding ink ribbons you appropriately use
cassette tapes.

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:10.420
You’ll always find several tapes next to
every save along with some scattered around

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:11.420
the estate.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:15.689
But even with this relatively generous supply,
you're still forced to save more sparingly

00:01:15.689 --> 00:01:17.360
than you did in normal mode.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:20.830
Autosaves are less frequent but not gone completely.

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:25.180
They will still happen in certain story moments
to save you the frustration of having to watch

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:34.590
unskippable cutscenes over and over again.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:39.420
Your first real challenge comes from the Mia
chainsaw fight which is significantly harder.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:44.060
It only takes 2 hits to kill you and even
worse Mia has a much larger health pool.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:46.799
With only 27 bullets every shot counts.

00:01:46.799 --> 00:01:51.620
I frequently found myself running out of ammo
and having to switch to the hatchet, which,

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:54.390
against a chainsaw…

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:55.720
well…

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:58.140
I had to do this fight 8 times.

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:05.090
It's a brutal opener but the fight is important
because it teaches you two things that will

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:26.510
help you survive Madhouse; dodging enemies,
and nailing those headshots.

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:29.390
After the dinner scene you have to avoid Jack
like usual.

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:34.370
While in normal I could cheez it and run from
Jack, hiding becomes so much more important

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:36.500
due to his increased damage.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:38.349
Ok time for the garage fight.

00:02:38.349 --> 00:02:42.010
Just gotta pick up the car key and… huh.

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:47.810
In a devious twist you must now find a lockpick
to open the box that holds the key.

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:50.260
In the main hall things start getting real
different.

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:53.150
There are now 3 of those cages that take Antique
Coins.

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:57.740
Two of them feature new attack and defense
boosts but the third has the Scorpion Key

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:00.489
in it, which was originally in the basement.

00:03:00.489 --> 00:03:04.020
If you have enough antique coins to unlock
the Scorpion key's cage right away, you can

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:08.239
use the key to bypass this shadow puzzle,
quickly get to the next save room, and get

00:03:08.239 --> 00:03:12.209
the shotgun early.

00:03:12.209 --> 00:03:15.870
But on the other hand you don’t actually
need the key to progress and I want to save

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:21.270
my coins, so let's go upstairs.

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:25.180
Oh right, remember how Jack shoots himself
and then dramatically reveals he’s still

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:26.570
alive in the bathroom?

00:03:26.570 --> 00:03:27.629
That doesn’t happen here.

00:03:27.629 --> 00:03:32.210
He shows up pretty much right away and he’s
pursues you more aggressively.

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:37.450
You know what?

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:40.950
Screw it!

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:45.790
let's just uh, let’s try the key.

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:49.710
Awe shoot.

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:53.630
Come on.

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:57.549
Come on.

00:03:57.549 --> 00:04:02.360
Ok just gotta run to the save room and eeeeeeeee

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:06.830
And there's the next big change, enemy placement
has moved and later game enemies now show

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:07.990
up right away.

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:12.709
This makes the basement trek terrifying all
over again, as you never know what will pop

00:04:12.709 --> 00:04:18.079
up and when.

00:04:18.079 --> 00:04:21.519
Fighting the molded is tough since they now
soak up way more bullets.

00:04:21.519 --> 00:04:24.190
I wasted all my ammo on just two of them.

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:30.490
Although this does make getting that critical
headshot all the more satisfying.

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:34.900
However the game actually balances this increased
difficulty out really well, as the basement

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:37.160
has fewer enemies than it did on normal.

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:41.100
The basement is also where I put the saving
system through its paces.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:44.870
You're given just enough cassettes to feel
like you can waste 1 or 2 if you need too

00:04:44.870 --> 00:04:48.150
but not so many that it removes the stress
of choosing to save.

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:50.580
If you play smart it won’t lead to frustration.

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:54.169
You should always save in a new slot though
just in case you need to reload.

00:04:54.169 --> 00:04:55.930
Item placement has also changed as well.

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:59.990
There are more coins to make up for the extra
cages but their locations are moved around.

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:03.930
Major items like repair kits and even some
weapons have been moved and made available

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:04.979
earlier.

00:05:04.979 --> 00:05:09.330
Basic items like ammo boxes have fewer bullets
and you’ll find far more Separating Agent

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:10.610
instead of Chem Fluid.

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:14.520
This means you’ll have to make tough choices
like sacrificing bullets so you can create

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:15.520
medicine.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:19.410
And this is when it clicked for me that madhouse
isn’t some brutal difficulty designed to

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:23.889
be punishing and “Harder”, but instead
changes up the way you play Resident Evil

00:05:23.889 --> 00:05:24.889
7.

00:05:24.889 --> 00:05:27.530
Enemy encounters are less frequent but much
harder.

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:31.690
Later game enemies show up earlier but so
do advanced weapons.

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:35.699
Limited saves add stress but you can manage
that stress by saving strategically.

00:05:35.699 --> 00:05:39.820
I also understand now why madhouse is unlocked
after you playthrough the game once.

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:43.470
The foreknowledge of upcoming events like
bosses is important in helping you decide

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:44.840
when to use a save.

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:48.570
But at the same time this knowledge is also
used against you as the game plays with your

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:53.880
expectations in smaller ways like enemy placement
so it can surprise and scare you all over

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:55.980
again.

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:59.830
So if you feel the desire to start playing
Resident Evil 7 again like I did, give madhouse

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:00.830
a try.

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:03.650
It does a great job making the experience
feel new again.

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:07.740
Plus beating it unlocks infinite ammo which
makes for some wonderful catharsis.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:11.740
I love talking about both Resident Evil 7
and games that have cool alternate modes so

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:15.350
if you want see more videos like this, make
sure to like it and subscribe to our YouTube

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:16.350
Channel.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:19.389
Also if you want to see more Resident Evil
7 videos, I put out one about what it's like

00:06:19.389 --> 00:06:21.830
to play the whole game in VR so check that
out.

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:22.550
Thanks for watching.

